<title>USA: Zeneca gets US FDA okay on accolate tabs.</title>
<headline>Zeneca gets US FDA okay on accolate tabs.</headline>
<dateline>WILMINGTON, Del. 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Zeneca Inc said on Thursday that the U.S. Food and Drug Administration has cleared Accolate tablets for the preventative and chronic treatment of asthma in adults and children 12 years of age and older.</p>
<p>Zeneca said Accolate, an oral medication, works by blocking the effect of leukotrienes, natural substances in the body that can contribute to asthma symptoms.</p>
<p>Accolate is the first leukotriene receptor antagonist, a new class of drugs, to receive FDA clearance.</p>
</text>
